# COMPONENT

## CbdSupport

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.cbdsupport

### DESCRIPTION

Textus CBD Support aggregates authoritative CAR and SAR catalogs and exposes component discovery, exact component detail, dependency, operation, and usage guidance for Component-Based Development.

# SERVICE

## CbdRetrieval

### DESCRIPTION

Read-only CBD operations intended for publication through MCP.

### OPERATION

#### searchComponents

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

ComponentSearchRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

ComponentSearchResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

Search configured CAR and SAR catalogs by requirement and optional identity, kind, version, and runtime constraints.

#### getComponent

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

ComponentLookupRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

ComponentLookupResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

Resolve one exact catalog component identity without inventing unavailable versions or metadata.

#### getUsage

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

ComponentUsageRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

ComponentUsageResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

Return generated contract references, operation summaries, documentation, and artifact evidence for one catalog component.

#### resolveDependencies

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

DependencyResolutionRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

DependencyResolutionResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

Return direct and bounded transitive dependency evidence for one catalog component, including unresolved paths and explicit version conflicts without choosing a winner.

#### listCatalogs

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

CatalogListRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

CatalogListResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

List authorized catalog sources, their current readiness, cache freshness, expiry, refresh-attempt state, and sanitized source-configuration warnings.

#### status

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

CbdStatusRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

CbdStatusResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

Report catalog readiness, selected snapshot counts, and degraded source state.

## CbdCatalogAdmin

### DESCRIPTION

Administrative catalog refresh operations. This service is never MCP ready.

### OPERATION

#### refreshCatalog

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

CatalogRefreshRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

CatalogRefreshResponse

##### DESCRIPTION

Refresh one configured catalog or all enabled catalogs while preserving the last known good snapshot on source failure.

# COMMAND

## CatalogRefreshRequest

### DESCRIPTION

Administrative request to refresh configured catalogs.

### ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| sourceId | CatalogSourceId | ? |

